    'th.spineT': 'What is spine?', 'th.spine': 'Shaft flexibility. A 1.94 lb (880 g) weight hangs from the middle of a shaft supported 28" apart: it bends X thousandths of an inch. In carbon a higher number = more flexible (1000 is softer than 400). Wood is rated in pounds: 40–45# is softer than 55–60#.',
    'th.paradoxT': 'The archer’s paradox', 'th.paradox': 'Even though the bow is in the way, the arrow flies straight because it flexes around the handle. That’s why an arrow must never be rigid: it needs just the right spine for your bow.',
    'th.fistmeleT': 'Fistmele (brace height)', 'th.fistmele': 'Distance from the deepest part of the grip to the string. High: shorter power stroke, less speed, more stability. Low: more speed, more instability (Manual). Stick to the maker’s value.',
    'th.gppT': 'Grains per pound (GPP)', 'th.gpp': 'Arrow weight ÷ draw weight. The Manual recommends 8–9 gr/lb minimum: lighter and the limbs absorb the energy (“dry fire”).',
